      "message": "Here you are allocating potentially a few times, and using bytes.Buffer when you don\u0027t need it. You can arrange to allocate exactly once:\n\nreasonForRevData :\u003d make([]byte, 0, 1 + len(sig.RevocationReasonText))\nreasonForRevData \u003d append(reasonForRevData, *sig.RevocationReason)\nreasonForRevData \u003d append(reasonForRevData, sig.RevocationReasonText...)\n\n(this works because of a special rule for append([]byte, string...) mentioned under https://golang.org/ref/spec#Appending_and_copying_slices)\n\nTo try it out: https://play.golang.org/p/wlfo94soo39",
